-- title:
--   Surjection of the deformation ring onto O^{nr}[[T]] at a smooth point
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and let $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring and a $\mathbb{Z}_q$-algebra, adically complete for the ideal generated by the image of $q$, that ideal being maximal, with algebraically closed residue field $k$. Let $\iota : W(\mathbb{F}_{q^2}) \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be a ring homomorphism and let $X_0$ be a two-dimensional commutative formal group law over $k$ equipped with an action of $W(\mathbb{F}_{q^2})$ and an endomorphism $\varpi$ with $\varpi\circ\varpi = [q]$ and $\varpi\circ[a] = [\varphi(a)]\circ\varpi$, which is special for the reduction of $\iota$ (its Lie algebra is the direct sum of the complementary invertible submodules `lieZero` and `lieOne`, on which $W(\mathbb{F}_{q^2})$ acts through the reduction of $\iota$ and through its Frobenius twist respectively) and whose $[q]$-kernel has degree $q^4$. Let $R$ be a local Noetherian $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra, complete for its maximal-ideal topology, let $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ be a ring homomorphism restricting to the residue map on $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, and let $X^u$ be a formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module over $R$ together with an isomorphism $w^u$ from its reduction along $\mathrm{res}_R$ to $X_0$. Assume the pro-representability hypothesis: for every Artinian local $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra $A$ with surjective $\mathrm{res}_A : A \to k$ restricting to the residue map, every formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-module $X$ over $A$ which is special for $\iota$ composed with $A$'s structure map and whose $[q]$-kernel has degree $q^4$, and every isomorphism $w$ from $X$'s reduction to $X_0$, there is a unique $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra map $\chi : R \to A$ with $\mathrm{res}_A \circ \chi = \mathrm{res}_R$ for which some isomorphism $v$ from the pushforward of $X^u$ along $\chi$ to $X$ satisfies that $v$ reduced, followed by $w$, has the same power series as $w^u$. Assume finally the smoothness hypothesis that the linear part of $\varpi$ does not annihilate both `lieZero` and `lieOne` of $X_0$. Then there exists a surjective $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra homomorphism $R \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}[[T]]$.
--
--   This is the smooth-point case of the local analysis of Drinfeld's deformation space of special formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules of height $4$: at a point where the linear part of $\varpi$ is non-zero on one of the two eigenlines of the Lie algebra, the universal deformation ring admits a one-parameter characteristic-zero quotient. It is used to bound the deformation ring from below, feeding into the statements that $R$ has Krull dimension at least two and that $R$ admits an algebra map with the prescribed behaviour on the maximal ideal.
